      "content": "thanks for those. they're a good start. i want to dig deeper though. one of the biggest things people in my community say is that this \"gentle\" approach is basically just an excuse for lazy parenting and that it's actually destroying the authority of the parent in the household. can you help me flesh out that specific argument? like, how does this trend scientifically or sociologically undermine parental authority and traditional family structures?",
